Every URL is opened automatically and a page that does not open counts as missing, so:
- Cite a page only if you know its exact URL. If you are not certain of the exact URL, choose a different source.
- Prefer Wikipedia articles and well-known reference pages: encyclopedias, university course pages, standards bodies
  and government agencies.
- Never build or guess a URL from a website's folder structure (e.g. company.com/products/<name>/). A company's own
  pages are fine only when you know the exact page.
